# Lets the interface's poller read published cluster metadata, and nothing else.
#
# The existing rules for this helper are granted to %sudo - the humans - and the
# comments in them say why an application identity must not ride along on an
# operator's rule: %haproxy-mgmt also holds the worker, and a service account
# must not gain a privilege because somebody else needed one. This is that
# separate decision, with its own rule.
#
# What it grants, exactly: run one helper, with no arguments at all. The helper
# accepts no argv and reads a bounded JSON request on stdin, which is what makes
# an exact rule possible - PRIVILEGE.md forbids wildcards in argument matching,
# and without the no-argument form a rule naming a cluster would need one.
#
# Every helper here writes nothing and takes no lock. The status helper reaches
# the nodes; the inventory helper reads the exact commit named by the published
# RELEASE stamp rather than a work tree; the cluster-list helper reads the
# cluster file. The readings helper (2026-10-08) answers the six manager-local
# readings in one call, by running their own helpers in its process: the
# version listing (saved commit metadata - number, date, comment - and the
# diffs asked for), the backup archives (directory metadata under the state
# backup root; it never opens an archive, which matters, because those hold
# password hashes and private SSH keys), the certificate list (metadata about
# the distribution root and certbot's renewals; private key material never
# reaches its output, because it parses the leaf certificate alone), the
# network description, the cluster settings and the stored objects. So the
# poller cannot choose what the interface is told is current, cannot show an
# unpublished draft as live, and cannot block a deploy.
#
# NOPASSWD because a service has no terminal to type a password at.
#
# Installed 0440 root:root, and accepted by visudo before it is put in place.

POLLER_USER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haprion/current/bin/haproxy-status-helper ""
POLLER_USER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haprion/current/bin/haproxy-inventory-helper ""
POLLER_USER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haprion/current/bin/haproxy-readings-helper ""
POLLER_USER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haprion/current/bin/haproxy-cluster-list-helper ""
